---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import ramsey from "../assets/ramsey.png";
import { profile } from "../data/social";
---

<section id="about" class="relative scroll-mt-44 px-4 py-28 md:py-36">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-14 md:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
    <div data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-balance font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink md:text-4xl">
        Curious about how systems learn, and how to ship them well.
      </h2>

      <div class="glass-shell relative mt-10 hidden w-full max-w-xs overflow-hidden rounded-[2rem] p-2 md:block">
        <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-[calc(2rem-0.5rem)]">
          <Image
            src={ramsey}
            alt={profile.name}
            width={480}
            height={560}
            class="aspect-[6/7] w-full object-cover grayscale-[15%] contrast-[1.05]"
          />
          <div
            class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0"
            style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent 55%, rgba(5,5,5,0.85) 100%), radial-gradient(120% 90% at 15% 0%, transparent 60%, var(--color-bg) 100%);"
          >
          </div>
          <div
            class="pointer-events-none absolute -inset-x-6 -top-10 h-40 rounded-full opacity-30 blur-3xl"
            style="background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--color-accent), transparent 70%);"
          >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120" class="flex flex-col gap-6 text-ink-muted">
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        I'm {profile.shortName}, a computer science student at {profile.school}. I build across
        two fronts: full-stack platforms and applied machine learning — federated learning,
        homomorphic encryption, computer vision — on one side, and the fast, secure network
        systems on the other, a habit left over from Cisco and Huawei certifications earlier on.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Outside of coursework, I build end-to-end projects to keep theory honest: models
        trained on real, messy data, wrapped in APIs and interfaces that make them usable. That
        habit has carried into this fall, where I'm working across three remote internships in
        parallel — research on document-vision restoration, a churn-modeling engagement, and a
        data-analyst role about to start.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        I care about the boring-but-critical parts too: clean data pipelines, reproducible
        experiments, and code that a teammate can actually read.
      </p>

      <div class="glass-shell glass-core mt-4 rounded-[1.75rem] p-6">
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
          <span class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">{profile.degree}</span><br />
          {profile.school} · {profile.location}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
